## IConversationHistoryTransformer

**Namespace**: `Cyrena.Contracts`
**Assembly**: `Cyrena.Core`

### Purpose
Used to modify the conversation history to ensure that context stays within limits. Kernel-locked (one instance per chat).

Replaces the obsolete `IPromptManager.ModifyKernelHistoryFunc` approach with a proper interface-based solution.

### Interface

```csharp
public interface IConversationHistoryTransformer
{
    /// <summary>
    /// Use to check post agent token streaming and apply changes to the persisted conversation history
    /// </summary>
    Task ApplyPostStreamModification(ChatHistory history);

    /// <summary>
    /// Allows modification of the history to be sent to the Kernel before assistant gets the message
    /// </summary>
    Task<ChatHistory> TransformPreIterationHistory(ChatHistory history);
}
```

### Abstract Base Class

```csharp
public abstract class ConversationHistoryTransformer : IConversationHistoryTransformer
{
    public virtual Task ApplyPostStreamModification(ChatHistory history)
    {
        return Task.CompletedTask;
    }

    public virtual Task<ChatHistory> TransformPreIterationHistory(ChatHistory history)
    {
        return Task.FromResult(history);
    }
}
```

### Methods

#### ApplyPostStreamModification(ChatHistory history)
Called after the model has finished streaming tokens. Use to apply changes to the persisted conversation history (e.g., summarization, pruning).

#### TransformPreIterationHistory(ChatHistory history)
Called before sending history to the kernel for the next iteration. Use to modify which messages are included (e.g., truncate to last N messages, filter by relevance).
- Returns: Modified `ChatHistory`

### Usage Example
```csharp
public class SlidingWindowTransformer : ConversationHistoryTransformer
{
    private readonly int _maxMessages;

    public SlidingWindowTransformer(int maxMessages = 20)
    {
        _maxMessages = maxMessages;
    }

    public override Task<ChatHistory> TransformPreIterationHistory(ChatHistory history)
    {
        // Keep only last N messages for the kernel
        var trimmed = new ChatHistory();
        foreach (var msg in history.TakeLast(_maxMessages))
            trimmed.Add(msg);
        return Task.FromResult(trimmed);
    }
}
```

### Related
